<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94804" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκηπτοῦχος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαπτ-</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῆπτον, ἔχω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bearing a staff, baton</i>, or
				<i>sceptre</i> as the badge of command, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. βασιλεύς</span> a <i>sceptred</i> king, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.231
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς τις ς. εἴη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.93
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ς</span>., of
			Aphrodite, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				55.11
			</span></i>; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρης] ἠνορέης ς</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Mart.</u>
				6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Subst., <i>wand-bearer</i>, a great officer in the
			Persian court, generally a eunuch, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ
				τύραννος ἢ ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Semon.
				7.69
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				7.3.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.1.38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.3.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.</u>
				1.6.11
			</span></i>; of Scythian princelings, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IPE</u>
				12.32<i>A</i>42
			</span></i> (Olbia, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>); later, of <i>beadles</i>
			at Ephesus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BMus.Inscr.</u>
				4.481
			</span></i>*.<i><span class="en">
				300
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ephes.</u>
				4(1)
			</span></i> No.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>.</div>
